    {
      "sample_index": 4,
      "text": "To solve this problem, let's first define what an angle's measure is. The measure of an angle is the amount of rotation from one side to another. In this case, we are given that the measure of an angle is double the measure of its complement. Let's call the angle's measure \\( x \\) degrees. Then, its complement will be \\( 90^\\circ - x \\) degrees. According to the problem, the measure of the angle is double the measure of its complement. We can write this relationship as:\n\n\\[ x = 2(90^\\circ - x) \\]\n\nNow, let's solve this equation step by step.\n\n1. Distribute the 2 on the right side of the equation:\n\n\\[ x = 2 \\cdot 90^\\circ - 2 \\cdot x \\]\n\n\\[ x = 180^\\circ - 2x \\]\n\n2. To isolate \\( x \\), add \\( 2x \\) to both sides of the equation:\n\n\\[ x + 2x = 180^\\circ \\]\n\n\\[ 3x = 180^\\circ \\]\n\n3. Divide both sides by 3:\n\n\\[ x = \\frac{180^\\circ}{3} \\]\n\n\\[ x = 60^\\circ \\]\n\nTherefore, the degree measure of the angle is \\(\\boxed{60^\\circ}\\).",
