      "text": "Let the measure of the angle be \\( x \\) degrees. The complement of this angle is \\( 90 - x \\) degrees. According to the problem, the angle is double the measure of its complement. This relationship can be expressed as:\n\\[ x = 2(90 - x) \\]\n\nTo solve for \\( x \\), we first distribute the 2 on the right side of the equation:\n\\[ x = 180 - 2x \\]\n\nNext, we add \\( 2x \\) to both sides of the equation to isolate the variable \\( x \\) on one side:\n\\[ x + 2x = 180 \\]\n\\[ 3x = 180 \\]\n\nNow, we divide both sides by 3 to solve for \\( x \\):\n\\[ x = \\frac{180}{3} \\]\n\\[ x = 60 \\]\n\nThus, the measure of the angle is \\( \\boxed{60} \\) degrees.",
